## 6. Hover Effects

The `:hover` pseudo-class is used to apply styles when the mouse pointer moves over an element.

### Syntax

```css
selector:hover {
    property: value;
}
```

### Example: Changing Color

```css
button {
    background-color: black;
    color: white;
}

button:hover {
    background-color: gray;
}
```

When the user moves the mouse over the button, its background color changes from black to gray.

### Example: Enlarging an Image

```css
img {
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}

img:hover {
    transform: scale(1.1);
}
```

The image becomes slightly larger when hovered over.

---

## 7. CSS Transition

The `transition` property makes changes in CSS happen smoothly instead of immediately.

### Syntax

```css
transition: property duration timing-function;
```

### Example

```css
.card {
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
}

.card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
}
```

- `transform` controls movement or scaling.
- `0.3s` defines the duration.
- `ease` controls the transition speed.
- `box-shadow` adds a shadow effect.

Transitions are commonly used for cards, buttons, links, images, and navigation menus.

---

## 8. CSS Transform

The `transform` property changes the position, size, rotation, or shape of an element without changing the normal document flow.

### Common Transform Functions

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `translate()` | Moves an element |
| `translateY()` | Moves an element vertically |
| `translateX()` | Moves an element horizontally |
| `scale()` | Changes the size |
| `rotate()` | Rotates an element |
| `skew()` | Slants an element |

### Example

```css
.card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
}
```

The card moves 5px upward when hovered.

```css
button:hover {
    transform: scale(1.05);
}
```

The button becomes slightly larger when hovered.

---

## 9. Combining Hover and Transition

Hover and transition are often used together to create interactive designs.

```css
.card {
    transition: 0.3s ease;
}

.card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
    box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
}
```

The transition property makes the movement and shadow change smoothly.

Without a transition, the hover effect happens instantly.

---

## Summary

- `font-family` changes the font style of text.
- `margin` creates space outside an element.
- `padding` creates space inside an element.
- Shorthand properties reduce repeated CSS code.
- `border-radius` changes the shape of corners and can create circular images.
- `object-fit` controls how an image fits within its dimensions.
- `:hover` applies styles when the mouse pointer is over an element.
- `transition` makes style changes smooth.
- `transform` moves, scales, rotates, or changes an element's shape.

These properties are important for creating attractive, readable, and interactive webpages using CSS.
